# Accepted findings for the Python 3.14 build unit, scoped to this family and nothing else. Both are
# reported from the CycloneDX BOM pip 26.2 ships at pip/_vendor/bom.cdx.json, and both are accepted
# only on the targets that must carry pip (builder, development, cli). The runtime uninstalls pip and
# is scanned with no ignore file, so putting an installer back into production fails the gate.
#
# pip 26.1.2, the version the upstream image ships, vendors the same two versions but ships no BOM,
# so it scans clean while carrying identical code. Pinning forward to 26.2 is deliberate: same risk,
# disclosed here instead of hidden by a scanner blind spot.
#
# Accepted 2026-08-11. Revisit when a pip release older than the 7-day cooldown vendors
# msgpack >= 1.2.1 and declares setuptools >= 78.1.1, then drop the entry and bump PIP_VERSION.

# msgpack 1.1.2, out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse. On disk at pip/_vendor/msgpack, backing the
# CacheControl HTTP cache, which PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1 disables in every image here. No pip release
# vendors the fixed 1.2.1.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools 70.3.0, path traversal in PackageIndex. Declared in pip's vendor manifest, but the
# package is not on disk: pip vendors only pkg_resources, and package_index.py is absent. A manifest
# artifact with no vulnerable code behind it.
CVE-2025-47273
